  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "We computed BONOBO co-expression networks for our 15 pig muscle samples and averaged them into one gene-gene network, saved as gene A, gene B, weight. Please run CONDOR on it to find communities of co-expressed genes."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"Please run CONDOR on it to find communities of co-expressed genes.\" -- I couldn't match this to anything a registered NetZoo workflow produces or lets you set. CONDOR gives: communities in one bipartite network, with regulator-side and gene-side memberships, by bipartite modularity. Each regulator's and gene's core score -- its share of its community's modularity -- to pick out each community's core nodes.\n\nI couldn't match this to a result any registered NetZoo workflow produces, so none is offered.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
